      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Two more pieces turn a spec into running containers."
        },
        {
          "text": "A new pod starts out with no node, and the scheduler watches for pods like that."
        },
        {
          "text": "It weighs free CPU and memory, plus any rules you've set, then picks a node."
        },
        {
          "text": "The kubelet on that node sees that the pod is now its job."
        },
        {
          "text": "It has the container runtime pull the image and start the containers."
        },
        {
          "text": "Then it reports back, so the API server always knows what's really running.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
